\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 2. Working Day Rules\
Rule 2.1\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Every working day has a target of:\

\f0\b 9 Hours
\f1\b0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Rule 2.2\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 The company policy considers 
\f0\b 9 hours inside the office, including lunch and breaks
\f1\b0 .\
Therefore,\

\f0\b No Break Timer
\f1\b0  will exist in MVP.\
Working Time = Clock Out \uc0\u8722  Clock In\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Rule 2.3\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Working hours begin only after a successful Clock In.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Rule 2.4\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Working hours stop immediately after Clock Out.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 3. Clock In Rules\
Rule 3.1\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 An employee can Clock In only once per working day.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Rule 3.2\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Clock In requires GPS verification.\
The application checks whether the employee is inside the configured office geofence.\
If inside the office radius\

\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Clock In succeeds.\
If outside the office radius\

\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Clock In is rejected.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

